  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "There are many groups that assign moderation roles to people, sometimes even dozens of people and many of them have a rule against muting or blocking those people.\n\nSince VRChat doesn't provide a way to tell who those people are, it's often impossible to follow these rules and users have moderation actions taken against them for it.\n\nIn my eyes, this is VRChat encouraging groups to violate the Community Guidelines:\n\n\"Any rules should be fair. They should be possible to follow, and they should follow the spirit of the VRChat Community Guidelines: No hate, no harm, no harassment.\"\n\nThis is unfair and creates very toxic environments.\n\nThere are some groups that will create a separate \"staff\" group, indicating what they are. But users shouldn't have to look through people's groups, especially with the amount of pornographic and other sexually explicit groups that are allowed to exist in this game.\n\nI think it would be good for everyone if users had a way to clearly see who the group instance moderators are.",
